7	/**
8	 * Structural guards over the CUSTOMER-FACING SERVER ACTIONS.
9	 *
10	 * These are the functions the portal calls to act on a customer's behalf, and
11	 * they are the widest attack surface in the product for one reason that is easy
12	 * to forget while reading them: **every export of a `"use server"` file is a
13	 * public network endpoint**. Not "callable from the page that imports it" —
14	 * callable by a stranger with curl. That property is what turned
15	 * `verifyTotpForUser` into an unauthenticated 2FA brute-force oracle
16	 * (QA-PRELAUNCH P0-2) and is why `lib/safe-next.ts` and `lib/totp-verify.ts`
17	 * exist as plain modules.
18	 *
19	 * A reviewer can hold that in their head for one file. Nobody holds it for
20	 * fifteen, forever, while adding a sixteenth. So it is asserted here instead.
21	 *
22	 * ── WHY THE SOURCE IS STRIPPED OF COMMENTS FIRST ─────────────────────────────
23	 * This codebase documents its incidents in the code, at length. A tripwire that
24	 * greps raw source for `assertNotImpersonating` matches the comment explaining
25	 * why the guard matters — so it passes on a function whose guard was deleted and
26	 * whose comment survived, which is the exact edit a careless refactor makes.
27	 * `stripComments` removes comments (and only comments) before anything is
28	 * matched, so every assertion below is about executable code.
29	 */
